EQC framework for all its products and services to ensure that users are served well and that this will continue to be the case as their needs evolve. The main goal of the EQC for CDS datasets function is to develop precise statements about data quality that pertain to well-identified use cases. Those statements, in combination with other documented information about the datasets, constitute a knowledge base that can help users to assess fitness for purpose, given their needs and requirements.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"ndN0p8tPbJ"}],"key":"p7bDrtDlDJ"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layers of evaluation and quality control","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"gtsCr3L6am"}],"identifier":"layers-of-evaluation-and-quality-control","label":"Layers of evaluation and quality control","html_id":"layers-of-evaluation-and-quality-control","implicit":true,"key":"GYE03G0PZ4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The revised EQC framework makes a distinction between quality assurance, quality assessment and fitness for purpose.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"lAJm3DaU9G"}],"key":"RutVNekL3U"},{"type":"grid","columns":[1,2,2,3],"children":[{"type":"card","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Quality assurance","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"HtEOrFhHOL"}],"key":"rkJEx3ZAMq"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"data quality checks against key requirements","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"UDFJC6YSK6"}],"key":"tOuuyrDxqE"}],"key":"UPCTjxUOIf"},{"type":"card","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🧭 Quality assessments","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"qu34OnsC5B"}],"key":"onH4jt8HFP"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"scientific assessments which answer user questions","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"CdbPrcb7rH"}],"key":"wdHZJ7KDQN"}],"key":"EixLlzQ5yy"},{"type":"card","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🏆 Fitness for purpose","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"nnkXZDTZnl"}],"key":"WQFfQtKAfo"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"deciding whether data is suitable for a particular use","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"R4V3OOn5Jz"}],"key":"rlIAXsKpvQ"}],"key":"wK555XWGN0"}],"key":"w5ajhOGYHQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In more detail, ","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"pm9ttsIbuY"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quality assurance","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"WPKjSpoP5l"}],"key":"cQHh8P5nXy"},{"type":"text","value":" serves to inform users that data, metadata and documentation comply with a well-defined set of verifiable technical requirements. It provides evidence that this compliance has been checked independently from the producers. Quality assurance for each CDS dataset is implemented by verifying a set of well-defined technical requirements associated with the dataset. Specific assessment criteria for the respective data streams (e.g. reanalysis, projections) are developed to account for the different nature of these and the different types of checks that may have to be applied to verify the requirement. The role of EQC evaluators is to check these criteria and document the outcome to users.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"YkD1ftgThy"}],"key":"Iz7nO2pY1m"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The purpose of ","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"swOfUlJ6dW"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"quality assessments","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"LE83maKZ1k"}],"key":"VuMzapQpqW"},{"type":"text","value":", on the other hand, is to provide science-based information about accuracy, uncertainties, sources of uncertainty, temporal consistency, strengths, and weaknesses of a dataset in the context of a realistic use cases.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"vpln6YOy5w"}],"key":"vIFlrQzTZJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"EQC evaluators are tasked with developing quality assessments that are designed to generate useful statements about fitness for purpose of CDS datasets. The assessments address concrete questions about data quality associated with real use cases. Many of the assessments are implemented in Jupyter notebooks that can be shared, re-used, and modified by users. Assessments can involve multiple CDS datasets and use other sources of reference data. Assessments must build on relevant scientific literature, including published documents developed by producers and users of the datasets.","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"SvwsrmDdm4"}],"key":"BiKcayGsTB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Taken together, the outcomes of these activities provide the key information needed to determine ","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"key":"TZfnn3WnTE"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"fitness for purpose","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"key":"NNe83nRk6E"}],"key":"jXvdHsHJWf"},{"type":"text","value":". This information supports users in determining whether the data is fit for their specific application.","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"key":"z4IwvrH0Pe"}],"key":"Ffjy3JpyVu"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quality assessments","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"o40ZIJ8usa"}],"identifier":"quality-assessments","label":"Quality assessments","html_id":"quality-assessments","implicit":true,"key":"c3Zbj5TpsW"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each quality assessment is comprised of","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"T6lQzxChFf"}],"key":"MGdjQEFxNL"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","posit